WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.802
 Britt, Forest,
congratulations.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.537
The strength of
your tactical blades

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.706
has landed you in the
third and final round

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:09.608
of this competition, which
means that you're both four

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:12.746
short foraging days shy of
the title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.848
champion and that
check for $10,000.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:17.283
All you need to do now
is make one of these.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.657
A Halligan bar.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.692
It is an iconic rescue tool.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:31.096
And here to tell you more about
it is Captain Brian Olith.

00:00:31.196 --> 00:00:33.199
 The Halligan bar to
the modern fire service

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.167
is the multipurpose tool.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.871
It is probably the most
important tool that's

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.139
carried on a fire truck
besides water and hose

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:41.674
and the firefighters themselves.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:42.708
 Good luck.

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:43.576
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:44.277
 Good luck, brother.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.844 line:14%
 Right on.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.648 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.416
 Today I'm going to start
forging the Halligan.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:54.253
I'm going to start at the fork
end and just work my way back.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.324
My plan for construction on
this Halligan is forge-weld,

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.325
Damascus billet.

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:01.127
Not only is that
going to add strength,

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:04.864
but it will lend a considerable
amount of aesthetic value

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:05.865
to this.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.733
Is this enough steel?

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.236
Yeah.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:13.139
The pressure of being
a retired fireman

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:16.008
and being tasked with making
the very first Halligan

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:18.110
on "Forged in Fire,"
that situation

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:21.246
is not lost on me by any means.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.749
If I think about it too
much, I could probably put

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:24.984
a lot of pressure on myself.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:28.020
But what I have control
over is my design

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.689
and I'm going to do it
the best that I can.

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:33.292 line:14%
This day is over.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.594 line:14%
Beginning of day two.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.196
Let's get that steel hot
beat the hell out of it.

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:38.731
What we're going to do
today is we're going

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.399
to work on forming the adze.

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:43.036
We're going to stretch
out the handle.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.837
Right now we're just getting
that handle stretched

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.405
out to give us our length.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.173
For firefighters,
you're going to want

00:01:48.273 --> 00:01:50.777
something with some
heft to it to grip it.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:55.682
So I'm just coming in here
and I'm squashing my corners

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:58.618
to give it an octagonal shape.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:01.420
It's really looking
like it's supposed to.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.456
I'm going to do some
grinding and cleanup

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.958
and make sure I don't
have any coal [inaudible]..

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.794
I got a lot done today.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.729
I'm down to forging
out the forks

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.863
and a little bit
of straightening

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:11.997
and then on to heat treat.

00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:13.666
Really feeling good about it.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.533
Woo hoo!

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.535
Life is good!

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.503
Life is good.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.805
 Day three, I'm ready
to get this thing forged

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:22.241
and get it quenched.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.311
Get my forks pretty
well shaped up.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.381
Start forging that pike
out and it's looking good.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.517
So now it's time to drip
the hole for the pike.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.819
There we go.

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:35.287
All right, that's a biggie.

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:39.759
Now all we have to do is
get the adze into place

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.194
and we're ready to quench.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.764
I get things up
to heat, go ahead

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:49.702
and put it in the quench tank,
and I've got too little oil.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.037
Oh, that's not good.

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:54.139
So now I've got an
incomplete quench.

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:55.808
The only part that's
really not hard

00:02:55.874 --> 00:02:59.945
is the really important part,
like the adze and the pike.

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:01.480
Hang on, re-quench on that.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.082
Everything's riding
on this being right.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.852
If this doesn't
work, I'm screwed.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:11.257
Much better.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.025
It's actually a
really good quench.

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.226
I'm happy.

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:15.661
It's a good thing
I'm retired because I

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:18.998 line:8%
don't know that I ever want
to see a Halligan again.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.232 line:8%
 Beginning of day
four, today were

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:23.102
going to forge out the forks.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:26.872
And there you have
it, boys and girls.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:28.341
Let's heat treat it.

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:32.011
This is hands down the largest
tool I've ever quenched.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.446
So what we're going
to end up doing

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.414
is we're going to heat
treat the front half,

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:39.051
flip it around, heat
treat the second half.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.486
Let's quench this beast.

00:03:43.388 --> 00:03:46.125
She's straight, I see no cracks.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.659
Let's quench the other half.

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:49.329
3, 2, 1.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:55.201
We have a successful quench.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:59.905
So, what we're going to
do is simulate a breach.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:02.442
[music playing]

00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:04.543
I'd say it works.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:09.615
 Bladesmiths, welcome to the
car crash extraction test.

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.585
To test your Halligan bars, I'm
going to take your Halligan bar

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.755
and try to rescue this dummy
inside this crashed car.

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:19.659
Now this is all about how well
your Halligan bars perform.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:23.863
It's time to find out if your
Halligan bars will rescue.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.265
To test your Halligan
bars, I'd like to introduce

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:30.670
firefighters Jim and Carl.

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:31.404
Welcome, gentlemen.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.538
Britt, you're first.

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:33.239
You ready?

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.575
 Grip it and rip it.

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:38.645
[music playing]

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.784
 Hit.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.852
Go!

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.956
[music playing]

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.393
 Hit.

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.694
Hit.

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:58.697
[music playing]

00:04:58.797 --> 00:05:00.132
 Nice

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.802
[music playing]

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:06.205
 All right.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:07.473
Britt, let's talk
about your Halligan bar

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.375
here based on the
firefighters' feedback.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.943
First stop, the bar.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:14.280
It's a little bit heavier
but it's manageable.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.882
When it comes to your spike
and your adze over here,

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.618
they function quite well
and they got the job done.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.254
Overall sir, it will rescue.

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:22.988
 Thank you, sir.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:23.856
 OK.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:24.724
Forest, your turn, sir.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:25.825
Are you ready?

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.026
 Well, we didn't get
dressed up for nothing.

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:29.762
 Clear.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.865
[music playing]

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.441
 Hit.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:42.107
Hit.

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:43.843
Hit.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.911
Hit.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.714
Hit it again.

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:51.016
Hit.

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:54.587
[music playing]

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:55.455
Hit.

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:03.596
 All right.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.365
Forest, let's talk about
your Halligan bar here.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:09.502
First up, it's a lighter
weight so it's easier to carry.

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:13.739
Now, the adze over here did
not penetrate nicely inside

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.975
and the reason for that is you
don't have a flat surface here.

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:19.445
Not having a flat surface here
when you're making impact,

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:21.313
it kind of shears
off to the side.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:23.916
But it was effective,
it worked, and more

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.151
importantly, it will rescue.

00:06:26.251 --> 00:06:27.486
 Congratulations, gentlemen.

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:29.655
Your Halligan bars have
passed our first test.

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.523
So now we've turned up the heat.

00:06:31.623 --> 00:06:33.159
This is our flaming tower test.

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:36.796
Now to test your Halligan bars,
Firefighter Steve and Captain

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:39.064
John are going to
take them and break

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:40.666
through this training door.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.068
Once they're through
that door, they'll

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:43.769
go up three flights
of stairs, use

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:46.205
your Halligan tool again
to bust out that window

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:47.640
to assist in the rescue.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.241
Now no one really knows
what's going to happen

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:50.609
in a rescue situation.

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:52.878
So to test that Halligan
tool one more time,

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:55.047
we're going to drop it from
that three story window.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:55.947
 Awesome.

00:06:56.014 --> 00:06:56.849
 All right.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.083
Britt, are you ready?

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:00.486
 Let's break it.

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:03.556
[music playing]

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:05.191
 Hit.

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.792
Hit.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:09.128
Hit.

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:12.198
[music playing]

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:30.249
FIREFIGHTER: Right on the edge.

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:32.117
 The biggest thing
was the forks.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.620
They're a little too thick.

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:37.623
 So Britt, first off, your
adze worked very nicely.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.125
But the width of your forks
was an issue since they're

00:07:40.192 --> 00:07:41.693
so thick right here.

00:07:41.793 --> 00:07:44.530
Kevin had a hard time getting
that into that doorjamb.

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:46.398
When every second
counts, you want

00:07:46.465 --> 00:07:47.700
that to pass right through.

00:07:47.766 --> 00:07:50.536
But overall, performed
well, took the fall

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.404
like a champ, good job.

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:53.271
 Thank you, sir.

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:54.172
 All right.

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:54.973
Forrest, you're up now.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:55.741
You ready?

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:58.043
 Yes, sir.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:01.880
[music playing]

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:02.715
 Hit.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:03.282
Hit.

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:04.116
Hit.

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:08.153
Hit.

00:08:08.253 --> 00:08:09.888
Good.

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:12.558
[music playing]

00:08:29.074 --> 00:08:31.043
 This hitting surface could
be a little bit bigger.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:32.211
 Right.

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:34.880
 My guys could miss
it a little bit.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:37.883
 So Forest, right off, the
Damascus was a nice touch.

00:08:37.949 --> 00:08:40.252
The forks got into that
door really easily,

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:44.623
but this corner should be sort
of a 90 degree with flats.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:47.226
That axe kind of
slid off a few times

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:50.296
and you really want a good
driving surface on this.

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:53.031
But all in all, it
survived, good job.

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:53.799
Well done.

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:55.167
 Thank you.

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:59.671
 Britt, Forest, this has been
an extremely tough competition.

00:08:59.738 --> 00:09:02.440
For the first time ever,
we asked smiths to go

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:04.309
back to their home
forges and make

00:09:04.409 --> 00:09:06.011
something other than a weapon .

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:08.613
And you've both proven
that you're Halligan tools

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.683
are "Forged in Fire" tough.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:15.454
However, only one of you can be
the "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:15.554 --> 00:09:17.089
And that champion is Britt.

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:19.891
Congratulations, you're the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:19.958 --> 00:09:23.129
Forest, unfortunately
your Halligan tool

00:09:23.229 --> 00:09:24.663
didn't make the cut.

00:09:24.763 --> 00:09:27.966
 Well Forest, you brought us
an attractive and functional

00:09:28.033 --> 00:09:29.001
rescue tool.

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:30.903
However, it's lack
of a defined corner

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:32.938
with flat striking
surfaces caused

00:09:33.038 --> 00:09:36.642
it to be a little less
effective than your competitors.

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:38.510
And that's why we're
letting you go.

00:09:38.577 --> 00:09:39.979
 It's all right.

00:09:40.045 --> 00:09:42.747
 Forest, you made a beautiful
Damascus Halligan tool.

00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.282
But at this time,
you're dismissed

00:09:44.349 --> 00:09:46.751
from the training area.

00:09:46.818 --> 00:09:47.953
Good job, brother.
- Thank you.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:48.920
 Good job.

00:09:48.987 --> 00:09:50.689
 Brit and mine
both performed well.

00:09:50.789 --> 00:09:54.059
It's just came down to some
very minor design decisions,

00:09:54.159 --> 00:09:56.962
and Britt made some better
decisions and I did.

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:59.999
I'm exceptionally proud of the
fact of being able to represent

00:10:00.066 --> 00:10:01.333
the fire department.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.702
Sorry I didn't come out on
top, guys, but you know what?

00:10:03.768 --> 00:10:06.004
We gave her a hell of a good go.

00:10:06.105 --> 00:10:09.141
[music playing]

00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:10.642
 Britt, congratulations.

00:10:10.709 --> 00:10:12.144
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:15.047
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:15.748
Good job, man.

00:10:15.848 --> 00:10:17.349
 Thank you, sir Thank you.

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:20.085
I am the "Forged in Fire"
champion and it feels amazing.

00:10:20.152 --> 00:10:22.087
I came in here confident that
I had a pretty good shot.

00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:24.390
Forest comes from the
fire service side,

00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:26.025
I come from the law
enforcement side.

00:10:26.091 --> 00:10:27.826
I thought he made
a beautiful tool.

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:31.063
I simply just made a
slightly better tool than he

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.564
did and brought the win.

00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:36.102
[music playing]

